WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Moderator: Open the renewals overview as you would before a leadership meeting.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Grace Lindqvist: I want to see renewals by quarter and which are at risk. I see a list. Why is this one at risk? There's a reason chip, that's helpful.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Grace Lindqvist: Compared with before, I can actually defend the score now. The reasons make it credible. I'd trust it more.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Moderator: What's missing?

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Grace Lindqvist: A summary I can share. I'd have to screenshot this for the board. I want a one-click, board-ready view with the story behind the numbers.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Grace Lindqvist: Reporting is still too manual. If my ops manager has to build a deck every quarter, that's a sign the tool isn't doing its job.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Grace Lindqvist: I want to see if the work is happening: who owns each risk and what's the plan. I see an owner here, which is good, but not a plan.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Moderator: How do you feel about the alerts?

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Grace Lindqvist: I don't want alerts. I want a weekly digest of what changed in my biggest accounts. Anything urgent can find me.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Grace Lindqvist: The handoff between support and success is the thing I worry about. Does a dropped ticket show up for the CSM? I'd feel safer if I could see handoffs in one place.

